<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baganda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ganda people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baganda, or Ganda, are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> people of central Uganda, the country's largest ethnic group, whose kingdom of Buganda lay on the northern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a>. In the late 19th century Ganda chiefs and soldiers allied with the British, fighting Bunyoro and serving as agents of colonial rule across the Uganda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>. Their language, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luganda">Luganda</a>, is widely spoken in Uganda.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baganda.jpg" alt="Baganda" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Buganda.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
